+python build/checkpoint_garage_reflections_drain.py
+```
+
+Results: reflection proof **145 Compatibility including 120 actual motion frames**, **25 desktop Mobile/Vulkan**, profile fixture **25**; reference layout/four sizes **25 + 25**; roof/fixed-platform/common-camera/drain-area contracts **38**, carousel/local cosmetics/frozen cards **175**, car transitions/retained zoom **23**, washing **1,402**, view controls **59**, exact car/glazing regression **80**; zero failures. Import passes. Turning the actual car changes the pedestal capture while preserving the real camera transform and condition. With reflections toggled off under the same pose/light, measured pedestal-region changed pixels are **14,438 Compatibility / 14,277 Mobile**; floor-region changed pixels **25,647 on each**. Tests also cover correct mirrored-camera winding/height, same-world source, capture bounds, replacement binding, hidden-page stop/resume, real inset drain and no cosmetic saves. The ordinary car remains 64 meshes/104,558 triangles/68,996 UV vertices with exact baked/source geometry and glazing bytes; no invariant assertion was removed or weakened.
+
+Final RTX 3090 Compatibility render-work sample, 120 measured rotating frames: main 1168x372, each reflection 584x186; sum of all three per-viewport timers CPU median/p95 **1.725/2.472ms**, GPU median/p95 **0.726/1.312ms**. These sums describe captured render work, not full application wall-frame timing, isolated incremental cost or phone performance. The normal model diagnostic separately measured 488.594ms cold construction and main-view-only CPU median/p95 0.873/1.267ms, GPU 0.791/2.688ms; its layout/pixel coverage differs from the aggregate sample, so do not interpret their difference as a speedup.
+
+Initial native cubemap probes produced broad highlights rather than sufficiently aligned car reflections and an engine texture-RID warning on one Mobile shutdown; that prototype was replaced entirely by these planar captures. Transparent backgrounds and explicit texture unbinding corrected the dark empty-surface contribution and avoided that shutdown warning in the final runs. The floor's periodic bump and fine drain brushing were removed after their moire became visible. Final captures use the revised geometry/materials and actual same-world reflection output.
+
+Inspected [normal garage](evidence/garage-reflections-drain-2026-10-12/overview/garage-1720.png), [floor/pedestal proof](evidence/garage-reflections-drain-2026-10-12/proof/reflections-on.png), [drain close-up](evidence/garage-reflections-drain-2026-10-12/proof/drain-closeup.png), turned/pickup/close-up states, off diagnostic and matching Mobile views. [Reflected full-turn motion](evidence/garage-reflections-drain-2026-10-12/reflected-turntable-motion.png) is a 120-frame 960x540 lossless APNG, approximately 45MB, assembled from actual Godot PNG frames using Python stdlib/CRC checks. Four-second 30fps playback is for review, not a performance measurement. Raw frames: `build/garage-reflection-motion-2026-10-12`.
+
+Task-only two-commit checkpoint: `build/garage_reflections_drain/checkpoint-repo`; baseline sources, scoped patch, hashes, captures and actual logs: `docs/evidence/garage-reflections-drain-2026-10-12`. Main branch/index and concurrent unrelated work are preserved. Same-world capture behavior and shader built-ins were checked against official [Viewport](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_viewport.html) and [spatial shader](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/spatial_shader.html) documentation and the pinned-renderer runs above.
+
+Doctor sees an attached DN2103 Android device. This build was **not exported, installed or tested on the phone**. No full Validate, physics merge/regression, backend operation or deployment was performed. Owner gloss/drain/style acceptance and physical-device frame pacing, memory, brightness and reflection readability remain open. AAA remains a quality target.
